STL -> STEP Converter — Usage Information
----------------------------------

Overview
This utility converts STL files to STEP. It can also split multi‑body STL files into separate bodies before conversion.

Quick Start
1) Select an input .stl file.
2) Select or enter an output .stp file path.
3) (Optional) Enable "Split bodies" to separate connected components.
4) Click Convert.

Notes
- When splitting is enabled, it is generally recommended to use a 
  separate output directory for each model.
- When splitting is enabled, individual body files are saved as
  <base>_body_<n>_tris<tianglecount>.stl and converted to <base>_body_<n>_tris<tianglecount>.stp.
  Stl files are saved in ASCII format.
  The original file is not modified.
- When splitting and 'Split, convert, open directory' is enabled, the
  resulting files are opened in the target directory.
- When splitting is not enabled, and 'Open STL after conversion' is 
  enabled, the resulting file is opened with the default application 
  for .stl files.
- Tolerance can be selected from the drop‑down if needed.
  It is generally recommended to use the default value.    
- Large STEP models may take time to open after conversion.


